## Location
`rust/lichen-schc/src/codec.rs` lines 440-447, 482-489, 530-538, 575-583, 649-656

## Issue
The same 5-line tail-copy pattern appears in compress_coap, compress_icmpv6_echo, compress_rpl_dio, compress_rpl_dao, compress_mqtt_sn:

```rust
let residue_len = w.byte_len();
let tail_start = 1 + residue_len;
let needed = tail_start + tail.len();
if needed > out.len() { return Err(BufferTooSmall::new(needed, out.len()).into()); }
out[tail_start..needed].copy_from_slice(tail);
Ok(needed)
```

## Suggested fix
Add a method to BitWriter that finalizes with a tail copy:

```rust
impl<'a> BitWriter<'a> {
    fn finalize_with_tail(&mut self, out: &mut [u8], tail: &[u8]) -> Result<usize, SchcError> {
        let residue_len = self.byte_len();
        let tail_start = 1 + residue_len;
        let needed = tail_start + tail.len();
        if needed > out.len() {
            return Err(BufferTooSmall::new(needed, out.len()).into());
        }
        out[tail_start..needed].copy_from_slice(tail);
        Ok(needed)
    }
}
```

## Impact
Reduces duplication, makes the compress functions more uniform, and centralizes buffer-overflow checking.
